	doi = {10.1086/185943},
	abstract = {H2CCC, an isomer of the widely distributed interstellar ring C3H2, has been detected in TMC-1 and possibly IRC + 10216 with the IRAM 30 m telescope, following a recent laboratory determination of the rotational spectrum of this new type of highly polar carbon chain. The rotational temperature of H2CCC in TMC-1, like that of other highly polar molecules in this source, is very low: 4-6 K; the column density is also fairly low: (2.5 + or - 0.5) x 10 to the 12th/sq cm, slightly more than 1 percent that of the cyclic isomer.},
